.TH "PB-CONFIG-STATUS-BAR-PREVIEW" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-status-bar-preview - Preview the configured status bar


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config status-bar preview [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Preview the configured status bar

.PP
Render the current status bar at the requested width without opening a remote session. Use it to check truncation and theme choices before connecting.

.PP
The status bar is rendered by the interactive terminal client. Preferences affect local presentation and do not change remote sessions. Use preview to inspect the result before relying on a theme or width setting.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for preview

.PP
\fB--width\fP=0
	preview width (20-500 columns)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-status-bar(1)\fP
